The failing line, in the image's own startup script
===================================================
$ grep -n 'hostname\|set -e' /dockerstartup/vnc_startup.sh
3:set -e
63:VNC_IP=$(hostname -i)

Line 63 asks the container for its own IP. There is no network yet, so it fails.
Line 3's `set -e` turns that into an immediate exit 1. The container dies, its
network namespace goes away, and the CNI chain then reports the Statfs error the
author actually sees.

Why it works when run by hand
=============================
Running the exact same script from a terminal in a healthy sandbox succeeds:

  VNCSERVER started on DISPLAY= :1
  => connect via VNC viewer with 10.0.250.2:5901

By then the container is on the network, so `hostname -i` resolves. That is why
the image looks fine on inspection and only fails at boot.

